---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Code of Conduct"
  description="The rules for CC3PO AI Builders sessions — what we expect, what we don't tolerate, and how to report a problem. CC3PO LLC."
>
  <div class="container wrap">
    <div class="badge">Policy</div>
    <h1>Code of Conduct</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      CC3PO AI Builders · CC3PO LLC · Last updated: November 2026
    </p>

    <h2>Who this applies to</h2>
    <p>
      Everyone at a CC3PO AI Builders session — attendees, presenters,
      sponsors, organizers, volunteers — and anyone acting on behalf of the
      program online. It applies before, during, and after events, in program
      spaces, and in program communications.
    </p>
    <p>
      This program is for adults. Attendees must be 18 or older. We do not
      admit minors to sessions, with or without a guardian.
    </p>
    <p>
      Admission requires an approved application or a named invitation. Each
      admission admits one named person and is personal and not transferable.
      There are no plus-ones, substitutions, shared credentials, or
      walk-ins. If you need accessibility support accompanying you, arrange it
      with the organizer in advance and it will be recorded separately for
      check-in.
    </p>

    <h2>What we expect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Be respectful, constructive, and professional.</li>
      <li>Focus on technical substance and good-faith discussion.</li>
      <li>Credit collaborators and sources. Describe your own role accurately. Don't claim someone else's work as your own.</li>
      <li>Be straightforward and honest. Share evidence and uncertainty openly. Change your view when the facts change.</li>
      <li>Disagree without personal attacks.</li>
      <li>Respect differences in background, experience, and perspective.</li>
      <li>Put the room first. Help the person next to you.</li>
      <li>Protect other people's data. Never bring client, employer, patient, or customer information into a session.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we don't tolerate</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Harassment, intimidation, or discrimination of any kind.</li>
      <li>Offensive comments about gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, ethnicity, national origin, religion, disability, age, or appearance.</li>
      <li>Sexual language, imagery, or unwanted advances.</li>
      <li>Deliberate disruption of sessions or demos.</li>
      <li>Recording or photographing anyone who has asked not to be photographed.</li>
      <li>Using another participant's work, code, or data without permission.</li>
      <li>Soliciting participants for your own paid services during a session. Talking about your business is fine and encouraged.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
    <p>
      If something happens that breaks this code, tell an organizer at the
      session, or email
      <a href="mailto:legal@cc3po.com">legal@cc3po.com</a>. You do not need
      to have the whole story, and you do not need to have already left.
      We take every report seriously, and we will not tell anyone who reported
      a problem who reported it.
    </p>

    <h2>What happens next</h2>
    <p>
      An organizer will talk to the people involved, usually separately. Then
      they will decide what to do. Depending on what happened, that can range
      from a quiet word to a permanent ban from the program. We will tell the
      person who reported what we decided, and we will tell the person who
      was reported what we decided and why.
    </p>

    <h2>Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      If something about the physical space, the schedule, or the format of a
      session makes it hard for you to take part, tell the organizer. We would
      rather adjust than lose you. Ask in advance if you can, but we will also
      accommodate on the day.
    </p>

    <h2>Language</h2>
    <p>
      Sessions are taught in English. Spanish materials are available. Se
      habla español — ask the organizer.
    </p>

    <p class="foot">
      CC3PO AI Builders · CC3PO LLC ·
      <a href="mailto:legal@cc3po.com">legal@cc3po.com</a> · 209-701-1137
    </p>
  </div>
  <Footer />
</Base>
<style>
  .wrap { padding: 90px 0 60px; max-width: 720px; }
  .badge {
    display: inline-block; background: rgba(16,185,129,0.1); color: var(--accent);
    border: 1px solid rgba(16,185,129,0.2); border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 6px 16px; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 22px;
  }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .lead { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 14px 0 34px; }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 36px 0 12px;
    color: var(--text); letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; margin: 12px 0; }
  ul { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; margin: 12px 0 12px 20px; }
  li { margin: 5px 0; }
  strong { color: var(--text); }
  a { color: var(--accent); }
  .foot {
    margin-top: 44px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-dim);
  }
</style>
